    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Paleoclimatology",
    "problem": "The specific processes driving large fluctuations in atmospheric methane during past glacial climate changes remain uncertain, as previous methods have been unable to provide a detailed, quantitative attribution of the contributions from individual sources like wetlands and biomass burning.",
    "method": "We use a new ice-core record of carbon isotopic ratios in methane to constrain a Monte Carlo box model, enabling the estimation of individual methane emission sources and atmospheric lifetime during the last glacial termination.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify past methane emission sources, specifically biomass burning and boreal wetlands, during the last glacial termination using a new ice core record of carbon isotopic ratios in methane to constrain a box model.",
